  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    # Find the two non-zero points\n    points = []\n    for r in range(len(grid)):\n        for c in range(len(grid[0])):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                points.append((r, c, grid[r][c]))\n    \n    r1, c1, v1 = points[0]\n    r2, c2, v2 = points[1]\n    \n    # Initialize output grid with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(len(grid[0]))] for _ in range(len(grid))]\n    \n    if r1 == r2:\n        # Horizontal alignment\n        if c1 > c2:\n            c1, c2 = c2, c1\n            v1, v2 = v2, v1\n        row = r1\n        d = c2 - c1\n        k = (d - 3) // 2\n        \n        # Left side (v1)\n        # Horizontal line from c1 to c1+k\n        for c in range(c1, c1 + k + 1):\n            output[row][c] = v1\n        # Vertical line at c1+k from row-2 to row+2\n        for r in range(row - 2, row + 3):\n            output[r][c1 + k] = v1\n        # Horizontal stubs extending right by 1\n        output[row - 2][c1 + k + 1] = v1\n        output[row + 2][c1 + k + 1] = v1\n        \n        # Right side (v2)\n        # Horizontal line from c2-k to c2\n        for c in range(c2 - k, c2 + 1):\n            output[row][c] = v2\n        # Vertical line at c2-k from row-2 to row+2\n        for r in range(row - 2, row + 3):\n            output[r][c2 - k] = v2\n        # Horizontal stubs extending left by 1\n        output[row - 2][c2 - k - 1] = v2\n        output[row + 2][c2 - k - 1] = v2\n        \n    else:\n        # Vertical alignment\n        if r1 > r2:\n            r1, r2 = r2, r1\n            v1, v2 = v2, v1\n        col = c1\n        d = r2 - r1\n        k = (d - 3) // 2\n        \n        # Top side (v1)\n        # Vertical line from r1 to r1+k\n        for r in range(r1, r1 + k + 1):\n            output[r][col] = v1\n        # Horizontal line at r1+k from col-2 to col+2\n        for c in range(col - 2, col + 3):\n            output[r1 + k][c] = v1\n        # Vertical stubs extending down by 1\n        output[r1 + k + 1][col - 2] = v1\n        output[r1 + k + 1][col + 2] = v1\n        \n        # Bottom side (v2)\n        # Vertical line from r2-k to r2\n        for r in range(r2 - k, r2 + 1):\n            output[r][col] = v2\n        # Horizontal line at r2-k from col-2 to col+2\n        for c in range(col - 2, col + 3):\n            output[r2 - k][c] = v2\n        # Vertical stubs extending up by 1\n        output[r2 - k - 1][col - 2] = v2\n        output[r2 - k - 1][col + 2] = v2\n    \n    return output\n```",
